Job Description & Summary&nbsp; 

Responsibilities: &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

- Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 
 - Application Modernization: Re-architect, containerize, and migrate monolithic applications into modern cloud or hybrid environments (Kubernetes, microservices). &nbsp; 
 - Infrastructure as Code (IaC): Design, build, and maintain cloud infrastructure and resources declaratively using Terraform. &nbsp; 
 - Configuration & Deployment Automation: Write and optimize Ansible playbooks and roles for automated server configuration, software deployment, and routine patch management. &nbsp; 
 - Reliability & Incident Management: Define and track SLOs, SLAs, and error budgets; build automated self-healing remediation workflows to reduce MTTR. &nbsp; 
 - CI/CD Integration: Integrate Terraform and Ansible pipelines into robust CI/CD workflows to guarantee consistent, zero-touch deployments. &nbsp; 
 - Security & Compliance: Ensure all infrastructure templates and configuration scripts adhere to enterprise security baselines and compliance policies. &nbsp; 
 - Required Skills & Qualifications&nbsp; 
 - Experience: 8+ years in SRE, DevOps, or Cloud Engineering focused on infrastructure automation and application modernization. &nbsp; 
 - Core Automation Stack: &nbsp; 
 - Expert-level proficiency in Terraform (State management, modules, and multi-cloud provisioning). &nbsp; 
 - Strong hands-on experience with Ansible (Playbooks, roles, idempotency, and agentless execution). &nbsp; 
 - Cloud & Container Technologies: Solid working experience with AWS/Azure/GCP, Docker, and Kubernetes (EKS/AKS/GKE). &nbsp; 
 - Scripting & Tooling: Proficient in Python or Bash, and experienced with Git-based version control workflows (GitLab CI, GitHub Actions). &nbsp; 
 - Observability: Familiarity with monitoring, logging, and tracing stacks (e. g. , Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog, ELK). &nbsp; 
